From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw89: add RTL8192XB support

The RTL8192XB is a 2T2R 2.4 GHz 802.11ax PCIe chip of the RTL8852C
family. It shares the MAC, the BB register map, the efuse map and most
BB glue with the RTL8852C, so it is built on rtw89_8852c_common, which
now also holds the efuse, phycap, thermal, gain offset, TX shape and TX
power unit code of both chips.

What differs, following Realtek's rtk_wifi6_ap driver:
- single band: TX DMA channels ACH0-3, CH8, CH9 and CH12 only, and the
  HFC quota of all pages in group 0;
- power on: no CMAC1, PC LDO ports on, P0/P1 isolation released, and a
  core voltage trim on T process dies without power calibration;
- ADC settings per bandwidth from the FT and ADC timing efuse codes;
- gain error, wideband AGC and front-end pin map of the eFEM RFE types;
- BB reset, CCK RX enable, T2R time and path-common values.

Calibration is limited to RCK for now. DPK is bypassed, as the vendor
driver does with an external PA. BB, RF and TX power tables come from
firmware elements.

Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/Kconfig
@@ -53,6 +53,11 @@ config RTW89_8852C
 	depends on m
 	select RTW89_8852C_COMMON
 
+config RTW89_8192XB
+	tristate
+	depends on m
+	select RTW89_8852C_COMMON
+
 config RTW89_8922A
 	tristate
 	depends on m
@@ -154,6 +159,16 @@ config RTW89_8852CE
 	help
 	  Select this option will enable support for 8852CE chipset
 
+config RTW89_8192XBE
+	tristate "Realtek 8192XBE PCI wireless network (Wi-Fi 6) adapter"
+	depends on m
+	depends on PCI
+	select RTW89_CORE
+	select RTW89_PCI
+	select RTW89_8192XB
+	help
+	  Select this option will enable support for 8192XBE chipset
+
 	  802.11ax PCIe wireless network (Wi-Fi 6E) adapter
 
